:: R5_MorningStandup [r5 story intimate]
<<location "Conference Room, Floor 39">>
<<objective "Get through the morning standup.">>

The standup meeting begins at 8:30. Seven people around the conference table. I sit down and the bra band tightens slightly and the chair back presses the clasp into my spine. A small point of pressure, metal through fabric through skin. I shift forward an inch. The pressure eases. The straps readjust.

Greg Tanaka runs through the project board. He calls on me for an update on the Waverly proposal. I stand. The straps pull. The cups lift slightly against my chest as my posture straightens.

<<sayself>>Waverly's due Thursday. Final projections are running through compliance. I've flagged the regulatory overhang in section three and proposed two hedge scenarios. Should be clean.<</sayself>>

Clean. The word tastes like a joke. I'm standing in a conference room delivering quarterly strategy while wearing a nude La Perla bra under my Brooks Brothers shirt and the only thing keeping me from visibly shaking is the fact that my legs are locked.

<<say "Greg Tanaka">>Good. Harper, take us through analytics.<</say>>

I sit. The clasp presses. I shift.

Harper Quinn stands. Navy blouse today, hair pulled back, a pen behind her ear she'll forget about for two hours. She runs through engagement metrics with the quiet confidence of someone who knows her numbers are bulletproof. I should be listening. I need to listen. The Waverly numbers tie into her trend analysis and I'll need the crosswalk for my Thursday meeting.

But the bra strap on my left shoulder has shifted slightly. It's sitting a quarter inch lower than the right. I can feel the asymmetry like a loose tooth you can't stop tonguing. My hand drifts to my shoulder.

I catch it. Force it down to the table. Flatten my palm against the wood.

Harper glances at me mid-sentence. Her eyes drop to my hand, flat and tense against the table, then back up to my face. She doesn't pause. She doesn't comment. But her pupils contract by a millimeter and something files itself behind her eyes.

I don't fix the strap for the next forty minutes. The asymmetry screams at me the entire time.

<<npc "harper" "suspicion" 3>>
<<modstat "officeSuspicion" 2>>

