:: R5_Side_Martin_Elevator [r5 sidequest]
<<set $flags.r5MartinElevator = true>>
<<scene "Elevator, Floor 39 to Lobby" "files/images/locations/r5-elevator-martin.png">>
<<portrait "files/images/characters/martin_hallway.png" "Martin Crane">>
<<objective "Get through the elevator ride.">>

Martin Crane in the elevator. Just the two of us. Nineteen floors of enforced proximity. He hits the lobby button. I hit 39.

<<say "Martin Crane">>Ashford.<</say>>

<<sayself>>Mr. Crane.<</sayself>>

<<say "Martin Crane">>Heard good things about your Waverly prep. Keep that up.<</say>>

He adjusts his cufflinks. Silver, heavy, monogrammed.

<<say "Martin Crane">>You know what separates the men who make partner from the men who don't?<</say>>

I wait. Martin doesn't ask questions. He delivers setups for his own answers.

<<say "Martin Crane">>Integrity. Not the ethics kind. The structural kind. Being the same thing all the way through, like a piece of wood. No hidden grain. No weak spots. You cut it open anywhere and you see the same material.<</say>>

The elevator passes floor 34. 33. 32.

I am standing next to a man who is lecturing me about structural integrity while I wear a bra and panties under my suit. The wood metaphor is exquisite. He's talking about having no hidden grain and I am hollow with secrets. I am so full of weak spots that I'm practically a screen door.

<<sayself>>I appreciate that, Mr. Crane.<</sayself>>

<<say "Martin Crane">>Martin.<</say>>

He corrects, which means I've crossed some invisible threshold. First names are currency at Meridian and Martin just slid one across the table.

<<sayself>>Martin.<</sayself>>

He nods. The elevator hits 39. The doors open. I step out.

<<say "Martin Crane">>Ashford.<</say>>

I turn back. He's holding the door open with one massive hand.

<<say "Martin Crane">>Whatever's going on with you. Sort it out. I'm on your side but I'm only on your side if there's a side to be on.<</say>>

The doors close. He descends. I stand in the hallway and wonder how many sides I have now and whether any of them face the same direction.

<<npc "martin" "suspicion" 3>>
<<npc "martin" "respect" 5>>

