</div>

:: R5_MartinLunch [r5 story]
<<scene "Partners' Dining Room, Floor 41" "files/images/locations/r5-martin-lunch-dining.png">>
<<portrait "files/images/characters/martin_hallway.png" "Martin Crane">>
<<objective "Get through lunch with Martin.">>

Martin Crane takes me to lunch. The partners' dining room, forty-first floor. White linen tablecloths. Heavy silver flatware that probably predates the building. Windows that turn the city into a postcard for people who can afford the stamp.

Martin orders a steak. I order salmon. He orders for both of us, actually, because Martin Crane orders for everyone at every table he's ever sat at. It's not rudeness. It's a worldview. Some men believe they know what you need before you do. Martin is the patron saint of that belief.

<<say "Martin Crane">>How's the Waverly prep?<</say>>

He cuts his steak with surgical precision. Even his eating is authoritative.

<<sayself>>On track. Compliance cleared the hedge scenarios this morning.<</sayself>>

<<say "Martin Crane">>Good. Good.<</say>>

He chews. Swallows. Points his knife at me, which is a Martin Crane punctuation mark, the conversational equivalent of an underline.

<<say "Martin Crane">>You've got potential, Ashford. I've been saying it to the partners. You keep your head down, you do the work. In five years you'll have my office. You know what that takes?<</say>>

<<sayself>>Focus.<</sayself>>

<<say "Martin Crane">>Consistency. Being the same man every day. The clients need to know what they're getting. No surprises. The firm needs to know what they're getting. No surprises.<</say>>

He leans forward. His eyes are grey and sharp and they miss nothing except the things they're not looking for.

<<say "Martin Crane">>Your wife. She good?<</say>>

<<sayself>>She's great.<</sayself>>

<<say "Martin Crane">>That matters. A stable home. A woman who supports you. That's the foundation. You don't build the tower without the foundation.<</say>>

I'm sitting across from a 55-year-old man who represents everything my father wanted me to become, and I'm nodding along to his theory of masculine architecture, and my ribs are encircled by a bra and my cock is cupped in lace and the straps on my shoulders are two thin lines of treason against every word he's saying.

<<say "Martin Crane">>You seem distracted today.<</say>>

He studies me the way he studies quarterly reports. Not with suspicion, but with the quiet certainty that any deviation from trend will eventually reveal its cause.

<<say "Martin Crane">>Something on your mind?<</say>>

<<sayself>>Just the Waverly timeline. Tight turnaround.<</sayself>>

He nods. Slow. The nod of a man who doesn't believe you but has decided to file it rather than press.

<<say "Martin Crane">>Eat your salmon. You look thin.<</say>>

I eat my salmon. The fork trembles once and I grip it harder. Under the table, I cross my legs, and the lace pulls tight, and my cock stirs, and I smile at Martin Crane and agree that consistency is the key to leadership.

<<npc "martin" "respect" 3>>
<<modstat "arousalRewiring" 2>>

